00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.430
So I'm an engineer
on the Firebase team.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.530
What is Firebase?

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:59.010
So Firebase is a suite of tools,
built on top of Google Cloud

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:05.800
at Google, for you to
develop applications faster,

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.620
better, stronger.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:12.660
And the idea here is that
we have developer tools.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.640
We have our backend services.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.120
We have tools for
monitoring app quality.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.570
We have tools to help you
grow your application.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:24.980
And then the all
important part is earning.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.360
You have tools to
help you monetize.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.380
So on the developing side, we
have the Realtime Database.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.600
If you're familiar
with Firebase,

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.430
that is the bread and butter.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:38.940
That was the product
that Google acquired.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:43.170
The Realtime Database
is a JSON store

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:48.660
that synchronizes in real time
to all your connected clients

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.010
over web sockets.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:51.690
It's pretty cool.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.880
This is a little bit
of an outdated slide.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.270
We actually have a new service
called Cloud Firestore, which

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.680
I'll jump into in a second.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.850
We also have user
authentication.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.870
This allows you to
sign in your users.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:06.770
This product is free.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:10.050
It integrates with
Google, GitHub, Facebook,

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:11.080
out-of-the-box.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:15.540
And then you can also provide
your own custom authenticators.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:19.690
So if you are in an
enterprise environment,

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:21.720
you can spin up
something that interacts

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.730
with your own backends.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:27.180
If you already have your own
custom authentication app,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.070
maybe something legacy,
maybe something you

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:33.120
still want to keep up, but you
want your mobile applications

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.950
to be using Firebase.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:38.880
Custom authentication lets
you integrate the two.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.410
We have hosting.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.420
We have Cloud Storage.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.930
So this is uploading binaries.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.560
Cloud Messaging.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.890
So Firebase Cloud Messaging
is the new version, basically,

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.400
of Google Cloud Messaging.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.940
It has a lot of new
features and it also

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:01.334
integrates with iOS,
which is pretty awesome.

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:03.000
And then there's a
remote configuration.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.260
And I'm a backend guy.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.500
I'm a developer,
so I like these.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.960
But there's also tools to help
you make your apps better,

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:11.460
right?

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.380
So there's the
Test Lab, where you

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.420
can submit your
applications that

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.250
will run robo tests on them.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:20.490
This is also in iOS now.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:22.740
We also have crash reporting.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:27.630
And recently, about year
ago, we acquired Fabric.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.960
So the industry standard
for crash reporting,

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:36.510
Crashlytics, is now
integrated into our toolset.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:39.450
We also have all of our
Grow products and Earn.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:42.570
I'm going to be coding for
you, so I'll skip over those.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.990
But if you need to grow your
products and some money,

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:49.100
check those out.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:54.370
So the idea with
Firebase, in general,

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:59.080
is we've actually written
the client SDKs for you.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:03.040
In a way, it's a
candy-coated Google Cloud.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.530
We built these tools for you.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.480
We built the SDK.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.210
We built the SDKs in
multiple languages.

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:16.220
It's iOS, Android, Web, C++,
Unity, all kinds of stuff.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:19.640
And the idea is that the shape
of the code looks the same.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:22.060
So when you go create
a web app and you're

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:27.490
calling the Realtime Database,
it looks similar to the iOS.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.390
Sure, the APIs may be
slightly different,

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:33.280
but the same shape
of the code applies.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.390
All of our client SDKs integrate
with Firebase authentication,

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:38.650
out-of-the-box.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:42.250
So you log in and
when it makes requests

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:45.980
against either Firestore
or the Realtime Database,

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:46.990
the user's logged in.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:48.790
You have those credentials.

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:49.790
It's instantaneous.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:54.250
It's magic, and it'll just
update the views on the page.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:55.720
They integrate with
security rules.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.340
This is very important.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:01.240
If you have a Firebase
project, maybe a demo project,

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.830
where you didn't
secure things, you

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:06.250
might have noticed us sending
out emails about this, scanning

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:09.140
for security rules.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:12.880
The idea is because
the client is directly

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:18.220
interacting with the database,
how do you do typical security?

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:23.110
If you had a REST server,
you'd, in the middle,

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:26.060
between your app
and your database,

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:29.260
do all kinds of checks
and verifications.

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:31.540
This is actually where
security rules come in.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:34.090
So it's JSON structure.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:35.670
You can go in there
and write rules

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:37.169
there are some great
examples there,

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:38.510
but I won't to touch on that.

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:41.180
But it's very, very important.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:46.939
And then finally, we added
this last year at Next.

00:05:46.939 --> 00:05:48.355
It's Cloud Functions
for Firebase.

00:05:48.355 --> 00:05:52.630
This has been the number
one, most requested feature

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:54.400
since it was a startup.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:58.709
Like forever was
cool, serverless.

00:05:58.709 --> 00:06:00.250
But I still need a
server because you

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.350
don't have compute, right?

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:04.870
So Cloud Functions
gives you a bunch

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:09.130
of neat little
hooks into Firebase,

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:13.660
and this is just a flavor on
top of Google Cloud Functions.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.240
So this is a Firebase
flavor, and it just

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:17.520
gives you extra hooks.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.830
You can listen to a path
in the Realtime Database.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:23.260
You can listen to a
path on Firestore.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:28.030
You can listen for
users being created.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:33.915
So Firestore is more like
a traditional database

00:06:33.915 --> 00:06:35.040
than the Realtime Database.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.870
If you used the
Realtime Database,

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.890
it's just a JSON store.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.200
There are some caveats.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.330
Querying isn't great.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.240
When you fetch
data, it goes deep.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:46.990
It gives you all the
data under that node.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:49.860
So it changes how you
structure your data.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:55.680
Firestore, we started on
this after the acquisition.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:00.330
We're like, well, how can the
cool things about Firebase

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:02.855
be brought to Google
Cloud technologies,

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:04.980
and the cool things about
Google Cloud technologies

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.350
be brought into Firebase?

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:10.200
It's kind of the peanut butter
and jelly of the Firebase

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:13.260
acquisition.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:16.200
And I will jump into
this a little bit.

