00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:06.650
along the way.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:08.530
So that's the
Angular application.

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:12.190
I actually did a little bit
of configuration ahead of time

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:15.490
on this, where I
just configured it

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:21.190
to bring in the Firebase SDKs.

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:24.760
So this is the
AngularFire2 library.

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:29.050
So with Firebase, we
have our main SDKs.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:32.150
So we have our iOS SDK.

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:33.310
We have our Android SDK.

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:35.620
We have our Unity SDKs.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:40.210
We also built, on top of
these, these smaller SDKs,

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:42.130
where they're basically
a compatibility

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:46.040
layer between whatever
framework you're developing in

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:47.710
and the main SDK.

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:52.390
So AngularFire is a library that
I'm one of the maintainers of.

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:59.440
And AngularFire tries to
make the Firebase JS SDK work

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:02.830
a little bit better
out-of-the-box with Angular.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:05.620
So that means things like
dependency, injection.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:08.080
That means things like
observables, rather than

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:08.860
promises.

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:12.620
And I'll touch on those when
I jump into the code more.

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:16.510
I also went ahead
