00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.340
So this is the Fire
Flutter library.

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:33.730
So similar to
AngularFire, we've built

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:39.040
just a little compatibility
shim on top of the SDKs.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:41.470
And what Fire
Flutter's going to do

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:44.230
is if you're building
for iOS, it's

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:46.390
going to be calling the iOS SDK.

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:49.270
It's going to do all the setups
and hookups for you there.

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:51.220
And if you're
using Android, it's

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:55.030
going to do the Gradle builds
and set up all the dependencies

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:55.930
there.

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:58.550
Who here has played
with Flutter?

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.300
Less people.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:00.800
All right.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:05.380
Flutter is a cross-platform
development environment--

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:08.850
so it's largely
targeting iOS, Android--

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:13.830
where you develop an
application in Dart,

00:11:13.830 --> 00:11:18.080
and it allows you to compile
for both iOS and Android

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:19.010
in the same code base.

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:20.220
It's actually really slick.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:26.570
So this actually show
the Flutter application.

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:38.800
So right now, I'm in
the Flutter directory,

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:43.300
and this is just straight
off the press, Flutter

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.590
initialized new application.

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:48.740
This is the directory structure.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:52.870
So here, we have
our dependencies.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:54.445
This is the main project route.

00:11:54.445 --> 00:11:56.270
Walks through all that.

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.730
Developer dependencies.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:11:59.860
Uses material design.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:03.370
It has a lot of nice
things built in there.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:06.580
But the meat and
potatoes of our code base

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:13.720
is actually just here,
simply in main.dart.

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:16.960
So we build our main,
our entry point.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.090
It runs the application.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.820
I build my app.

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:26.790
There's a stateful widget.

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:27.820
That's my home page.

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:35.569
And then there's a
home page state here,

00:12:35.569 --> 00:12:36.860
which actually holds the state.

