00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:23.960
The cool thing about Flutter
is it's actually compiling down

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:25.610
to the native byte code.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:29.474
There's no performance loss
because it's JavaScript,

00:13:29.474 --> 00:13:30.890
or something like
that, where it's

00:13:30.890 --> 00:13:32.780
going through an interpreter.

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:34.770
This is actually rate
to the byte code.

00:13:34.770 --> 00:13:40.100
It compiles to a native
Android and iOS application.

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:43.810
So that just spun up.

